{
  "requirement": "Without a configured agent, awaiting returns\n`ValidationError::NoAgentConfigured`. It invokes no provider, resolves and\nrenders no queued node insertions, and fabricates no response. If the callback\npropagates the error, the runner reports it without storing a completed\njudgment. Deterministic validations need no separate callback trait.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The two marked tests cover each obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.model_capability`.\n\n- **Returns `NoAgentConfigured`.** In `dropped_builders_and_missing_agents_do_not_resolve_queued_inputs`, `ValidationContext::new` has no agent. Awaiting `ask::<Answer>().successors_content(7).current_node_contents()` returns `Err(ValidationError::NoAgentConfigured)`. In `runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls`, the same error comes out of the callback through `Validator::verify`.\n- **No queued node insertions resolved or rendered, and no provider invoked.** The first test asserts that `Memory` recorded no `reads` and no `selections`. `fail_edges` is set for node 1, so any attempt to resolve the successors insertion would have produced a `Graph(\"edges\")` error instead. The no-agent context has no renderer or provider to call. The same test also drops a builder with queued insertions without awaiting it, and `ctx.inspection().dependencies()` stays empty.\n- **No fabricated response.** Both tests expect `Err`, and neither accepts an `Ok` value.\n- **Runner reports the error and stores no completed judgment.** `runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls` has the callback propagate the error with `ask_in_callback: true`. It asserts `verify` returns `Err(ValidationError::NoAgentConfigured)`, `state.records` is empty, and `state.reads` is empty.\n- **Positive control.** After `with_agent`, the same verification succeeds. It stores a record with only the `Dependency::Node` dependency, and the agent is called twice. This shows the earlier failure was caused by the missing agent.\n- **\"Deterministic validations need no separate callback trait.\"** This is a design statement. The tests use a single `Validator` callback (`run_review`) without a separate agent trait, and the clause has no behavior that a test could check.\n\nI found no unexercised obligation or boundary case, so I found no test-adequacy gap.",
